# Omnical — router-dav build & deploy repo
#
# Context: this repo was reconstructed fresh on 2026-09-28 (PLAN_DEPLOYMENTS.md
# §5, Workstream 0). The previous history tracked 33,998 build artefacts and
# two sets of LIVE SECRETS (a Let's Encrypt private key in out/tls/, and 15
# real CalDAV/CardDAV app tokens in out/omnical-iphone.mobileconfig). It is
# archived at ~/omnical-archive/router-dav-dotgit-2026-09-28 and the secrets
# are rotated on a schedule — see the "deferred rotation" runbook at the end
# of PLAN_DEPLOYMENTS.md §18.
#
# RULE OF THUMB: if it is a build product or a credential, it does not belong
# in git. The repo must stay publishable, because AGPL-3.0 §13 requires us to
# offer the running source to network users (PLAN_DEPLOYMENTS.md §10).

# ─── Rust build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CARGO_TARGET_DIR scratch (build-rust.sh:33). This alone was 33,377 tracked
# files and ~3.3 GB of .git.
/build/cargo-target/
/build/**/cargo-target/

# Any target/ dir. rustical/ is a submodule so it has its own ignore rules;
# these cover dav-tls/ and anything else in-tree.
/target/
**/target/

# zig-CC build leftovers (the legacy TOOLCHAIN=zig path)
/zig-cache/
/.zig-cache/

# ─── Build & release artefacts (out/) ───────────────────────────────────────
# EVERYTHING in out/ is either a compiled binary or a live credential. There is
# nothing in it worth tracking:
#   out/rustical, out/dav-tls              compiled, UPX-packed binaries
#   out/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/          compiled host smoke-test binaries
#   out/tls/{key,fullchain}.pem            LIVE Let's Encrypt private key
#   out/*.mobileconfig                     15 LIVE CalDAV/CardDAV app tokens
/out/
# Distribution + release staging (PLAN_DEPLOYMENTS.md §5.4 release.yml)
/dist/
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.sha256
*.sig
*.pem.bak

# ─── Credentials ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secrets never touch this repo. render-router-config.sh renders SMTP/IMAP
# passwords straight to stdout so they are piped into the destination and never
# land on the operator's disk (see its header, lines 9-12) — keep it that way.
/secrets/
/pass/
*.age
*.gpg
*.kdbx
.env
.env.*

# Private keys, in any directory.
/*.key
/**/*.key
*.key.pem

# Certificate material is ignored by default. The ONE exception is the public
# Sectigo intermediate CA that deploy.sh pushes to /etc/rustical/certs/ — it is
# a trust anchor, not a secret, and the app needs it to poll imap.novo-ordo.com
# (its server omits the intermediate, so every poll fails with UnknownIssuer —
# documented in render-router-config.sh:44-50 and referenced by the ca_file
# column there). Dropping it from the tree breaks inbound iMIP reply ingestion.
*.pem
*.crt
!router/etc/rustical/certs/*.pem

# Stashed-away copies of a previous .git. The pre-2026-09-28 history is kept at
# ~/omnical-archive/router-dav-dotgit-2026-09-28 — NEVER leave a .git.old* (or
# any other nested .git) inside the working tree, or `git add -A` will spend
# minutes trying to stage 33,998 objects of it.
/.git.old*/
/.git.*.old*/
/**/.git.old*/

# ─── Editor / OS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─── Appliance firmware staging (PLAN §9.2, item 12) ───────────────────────
# scripts/build-firmware.sh stages the payload into the package's files/ dir so
# the OpenWrt recipe has something to install. Those are the SAME build products
# as out/ (a 4.85 MiB UPX'd binary and a 610 KB one), so they are ignored for
# the same reason out/ is: a compiled binary does not belong in git, and this
# repo has to stay publishable for AGPL §13.
#
# The committed tree holds the recipe, the postinst, the sysupgrade keep list and
# the build script — all text, all reviewable, all gated by
# scripts/firmware-gate.sh.
/packaging/firmware/omnical/files/rustical
/packaging/firmware/omnical/files/dav-tls
/packaging/firmware/omnical/files/rustical-watchdog
/packaging/firmware/omnical/files/config.toml
/packaging/firmware/omnical/files/init.d/

# Credential-rotation drill output (PLAN_DEPLOYMENTS.md §5.2 item 1).
# These are `rustical backup` archives and their manifests — i.e. a copy of the
# production database sitting in the working tree at the exact moment someone is
# handling live customer data. Untracked is not enough; a single `git add -A`
# during a maintenance window would publish it.
rotation-drills/
.drill-protected
